.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_DETECT_SCRIPT
Deprecated explicit legacy host-detector override. The executable must accept
.B --json --no-prompt
and emit the historical host-facts JSON contract. Normal host detection is
implemented natively in Go and does not require this variable.
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_MANIFEST
Path to the personal manifest file, overriding the default XDG discovery
(\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/depengine/manifest.toml\fR, or
\fB~/.config/depengine/manifest.toml\fR if unset).
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_CACHE_MAX_BYTES
Maximum download-cache size in bytes. Defaults to 1 GiB; set to \fB0\fR
to disable automatic eviction. Invalid values fall back to the default.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the personal manifest. The default manifest path is
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/depengine/manifest.toml\fR, falling back to
\fB~/.config/depengine/manifest.toml\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for downloaded artifact cache entries. The cache is stored at
\fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/depengine/downloads\fR, falling back to
\fB~/.cache/depengine/downloads\fR.
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN
GitHub authentication token used for API resolution and private release-asset
downloads. \fBGITHUB_TOKEN\fR takes precedence over \fBGH_TOKEN\fR. If neither
is set, depengine may use an authenticated GitHub CLI.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI styling when set to a non-empty value.
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
Force ANSI styling for color-capable output when set, unless \fBNO_COLOR\fR
is non-empty or \fBTERM=dumb\fR.
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_TRACE_ID
Trace ID propagated to subprocesses for correlated logging.
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_LOG_JSON
Set to \fB1\fR to enable JSON output for the structured logger.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the state file. The state file is stored at
\fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/depengine/state.json\fR, falling back to
\fB~/.local/state/depengine/state.json\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B schema.toml
The declarative schema describing tools and installation methods.
Shipped with the project as a reference template.
.TP
.BI $XDG_STATE_HOME/depengine/state.json
State file tracking which tools were installed, by which method, and
when. Used by the
.B status
and
.B remove
commands.
.TP
.B scripts/depengine-completion.bash
.B scripts/depengine-completion.zsh
.B scripts/depengine-completion.fish
Shell completion scripts emitted by the
.B completion
command.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
0
Success — all tools installed or already present.
.TP
1
Some tool failed to install, or strict-mode validation found warnings.
.TP
2
Schema error — invalid TOML, validation failure, unknown method, or
unknown placeholder.
.TP
3
Runtime error — subprocess, state I/O, filesystem, or other infrastructure
failure.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
The project README and
.B docs/cheatsheet.md
contain the complete
.B schema.toml
reference, method examples, and placeholder documentation.
